WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.250
Hey guys, Pete here. Today I'm going to
try to answer some of the lingering

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:09.059
questions about Dark season three's
ending. At this point I've had a few days

00:00:09.059 --> 00:00:12.660
to sit with it and think about all the
questions people are asking in the

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:16.920
comments of my previous videos. I've been
rewatching with all these questions in

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:20.789
mind and I have answers for a few of
them. Before I get into them I should

00:00:20.789 --> 00:00:25.590
stress a couple things though. First, as
is custom, this video will contain

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:30.060
spoilers about the ending of the Dark
series. If you haven't watched all three

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:34.410
seasons in their entirety this is your
chance to leave. Second, I'm not a

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:38.820
scientist, but I'm also aware of the fact
that I'm not a scientist. These are

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:43.440
theories based on what the show's
writers chose to present to us on screen.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:48.149
The ending is open to interpretation and
personally I haven't seen a cohesive

00:00:48.149 --> 00:00:51.780
explanation for everything that I've
been able to jump completely on board

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:56.550
with yet. That said there have been three
questions that keep coming up and in

00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:01.199
this video I'll share the answers I've
arrived at after investigating the clues

00:01:01.199 --> 00:01:06.659
that the storytellers provided. through
the lens of my limited understanding of

00:01:06.659 --> 00:01:11.729
the theoretical physics of time travel
and quantum mechanics. The three questions

00:01:11.729 --> 00:01:17.310
are: 1. How did Claudia know
about the origin world? 2. How

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:22.439
was she able to set things in motion to
change the outcome in Adam and Eva's

00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:27.509
worlds? And finally, how could Jonas
and Martha stop the car crash in the

00:01:27.509 --> 00:01:31.619
origin world if that's what led to their
existence in the first place?

00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:36.240
The answer to the first question, how did
Claudia know about the origin world, is

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.470
something I feel pretty confident about.
Claudia's motivation has been presented

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:46.079
as wanting to save her daughter Regina
who gets cancer in Adam and Eva's worlds.

00:01:46.079 --> 00:01:50.729
The oldest version of Claudia has been a
mysterious character because prior to

00:01:50.729 --> 00:01:54.899
season 3 we didn't know what she was
really trying to do, and what made her

00:01:54.899 --> 00:01:59.670
that way in the 33 years of traveling
she did after surviving the apocalypse

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:05.130
in the bunker. Season 3 provided those
answers. She is in fact trying to save

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:09.810
Regina. In that 33 years she realizes
that no one can really change anything

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:13.920
inside the two world closed loop system.
Adam asks

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:18.569
her the question directly in the finale - 
how she knows about the origin world. She

00:02:18.569 --> 00:02:23.910
answers, "I spent 33 years looking for
answers in your world and hers. I've

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.050
tried to put together the pieces of the
puzzle. To understand how everything can

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:32.910
be reborn from the same family tree over
and over again until I realized that

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:37.530
we're not all part of a knot." She then
refers to Adam and Eva's worlds as a

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:42.569
cancer that must have grown from
something else. The origin world. She put

00:02:42.569 --> 00:02:47.160
together that all of the characters from
the Jonas and alt Martha's line wouldn't

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:52.080
exist in the origin world because they
all were born due to time travel. From

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:55.799
there she can eliminate characters from
the family tree and look for possible

00:02:55.799 --> 00:03:00.299
candidates out of who's left. When you
look at it this way it's not hard to see

00:03:00.299 --> 00:03:05.790
how she landed on Tannhaus as the most
likely source. Was it her parents Doris

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:11.670
and Egon Tiedemann? Was that Katharina's
parents Herman and Helene Albers. Or,

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:16.739
was it the guy who lost his family in a
car accident that also seems uniquely

00:03:16.739 --> 00:03:20.880
capable of helping them develop the
time-traveling machine? When she stripped

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:24.840
away all of the characters that are
direct descendants of Martha and Jonas I

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:29.160
feel confident that she would be able to
figure out that Tannhaus was connected

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:33.420
to the origin. that leads directly into
the next question. now that she knows

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:37.170
about the origin world how did she
manage to set things in motion to

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:41.340
reverse what happened there and thus
change the outcomes of things and Adam

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:46.950
and Eva's worlds? this is a more difficult
question to answer, but let's look at

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:50.850
what the writers have been telling us. in
the first season we learned that time

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:55.260
travel is possible and that the past and
future are connected. everything is

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:59.940
connected .everything affects everything
else. we see how characters struggle with

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:04.739
this and how human nature drives them to
want to change things. in season two we

00:04:04.739 --> 00:04:09.239
learn more about causal determinism and
we add the idea of the bootstrap paradox.

00:04:09.239 --> 00:04:14.069
the determinism angle tells us that
nothing can be changed and that no one

00:04:14.069 --> 00:04:18.539
has free will. the bootstrap paradox
explains how some things can exist in

00:04:18.539 --> 00:04:22.650
the world because of time travel and
have no discernable origin point. they

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:26.159
exist but we don't know how they came
into existence besides the fact that

00:04:26.159 --> 00:04:30.300
they travelled through time. season three
introduced the idea that Eva

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:34.590
describes as quantum entanglement. the
show defines this as a phenomenon that

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:39.690
leads to overlapping realities. basically
during the apocalypse there's a short

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:44.130
period of time that the chain of cause
and effect we learned about in the first

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:49.170
two seasons breaks down. in that instant
there is the possibility for reality to

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:53.430
go in two different directions and Eva
illustrates this to her younger self by

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:58.350
drawing the infinity symbol. at the
center of that you can see two realities

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:02.370
can follow two paths in different
directions and still end up back in the

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:05.580
same place.
the other concept Season three gives us

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:10.050
is the thought experiment of
Schrodinger's cat. Origin world Tannhaus

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:13.160
explains to us that the cat inside the
box

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:18.420
simultaneously exists in both of its
possible states, alive and dead, until

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:22.530
it's observed. from there he goes on to
ask the question of whether it would be

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:27.900
possible for multiple realities to exist
side by side. as far as Dark is concerned the

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:32.460
answer is absolutely yes.
we see Adam and Eva's world existing

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:37.680
side-by-side and Eva takes it further by
exploiting the quantum entanglement. she

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:42.330
forces two overlapping realities to
exist simultaneously. one where Adam

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:47.430
kills Martha and her unborn child, and one
where Jonas dies so that Martha can give

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:51.300
birth to the Unknown. when you think
about quantum entanglement and

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:56.010
introducing it to the story it makes you
wonder what all the determinism stuff

00:05:56.010 --> 00:06:00.990
was about in the first two seasons. well,
I think that when Origin world Tannhaus

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:05.970
created his time machine the end result
was that he split time and created Adam

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:10.020
and Eva's worlds. they are in fact
deterministic systems where nothing can

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:15.030
be changed. everything that happens has
already been decided and I think this is

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:19.140
backed up by the bootstraps artifacts
and characters that we know couldn't

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:23.370
possibly exist without time-travel.
Claudia explains to Adam that this will

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:26.880
always turn out this way.
Jonas and Martha will always meet and

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:30.870
she'll become pregnant. that will lead to
the Unknown being born and he'll

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:35.070
continue to make sure the apocalypses happen so that the material necessary

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:39.930
for time travel will be created. he will
always impregnate agnes nielsen in both

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:44.340
worlds which will always lead
all these characters being born. Adam

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:49.020
will always try to destroy that not and
Eva will always split the realities so

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:52.440
that she can preserve it. what that says
about Claudia's role is up for debate.

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:57.090
when she visits Adam she believes it's
the first time that happened. based on

00:06:57.090 --> 00:07:02.070
the quantum entanglement idea they
introduced she uses Eva's exploit to

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:06.150
split from her reality that takes her
back in time to continue the loop and

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:10.410
eventually get killed by Noah.
simultaneously in the second reality she

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:14.520
goes to visit Adam and that sets off the
chain of events that leads Jonas and

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:18.450
Martha to stop the car crash. I think
there's a strong argument that could be

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:22.500
made that this always happens as well.
the other concept they introduced,

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:27.960
Schrodinger's cat, is reliant on all
possible outcomes existing until the cat

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:32.880
is observed. and I think here is where I
will diverge from calling it the origin

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:37.710
world to calling it the origin reality.
we could think of Tannhaus' origin

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:43.140
reality as a place that can exist in two
states. one where his family dies and one

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:47.670
where they live. in the one where they
die he builds a time machine that splits

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:52.200
time to create Adam and Eva's
deterministic worlds and things

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:56.520
eventually loop around until they reach
the point where they cross over. I think

00:07:56.520 --> 00:08:00.390
based on how the story was written and
how the information was presented to us

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:04.680
we can think of the Jonas and Martha as
the observer in the thought experiment

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:08.970
that Tannhaus describes at the
beginning of episode 7. when they observe

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:14.310
Marek and Sonja turning around and thus
surviving, that forces the origin reality

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:19.680
into a definite state. they survive. Tannhaus never creates a time machine and

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:27.990
that forces the origin reality into a definite state. for me that
answers the last question on the list,

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:31.980
how could Jonas and Martha stop the
car crashed in the origin world if

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:35.580
that's what led to their existence in
the first place? I think the story is

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:40.320
telling us that Jonas and Martha are what
I can only think to describe as quantum

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:45.300
time travelers and their actions in the
origin reality forced the linear time

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:50.070
line there where Tannhaus family lives.
the only people that can exist in that

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:53.279
reality are people who were never born
from

00:08:53.279 --> 00:08:57.629
Jonas and Martha's line and I think this
is all wrapped up pretty well whenever

00:08:57.629 --> 00:09:02.430
they showed the dinner scene and close
out the series that way. so Claudia's

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:07.170
discovering the origin world figuring
out how the knot was constructed and

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:12.689
then utilizing Eva's exploit guarantees
that this is how this reality will play

00:09:12.689 --> 00:09:18.120
out. again I think this all adds up to
the storytellers telling us that this

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:23.579
isn't part of a bigger loop because that
state of the Tannhaus' family dying no

00:09:23.579 --> 00:09:27.600
longer exists. it is open to our
interpretation though and there's a lot

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:32.100
of different ways you can go. I like this
one. I think it's a good idea for how you

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:36.959
can take something that presents that
deterministic system but also provides a

00:09:36.959 --> 00:09:42.240
way for things to change. without Claudia
using the exploit essentially the only

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:46.920
ending that exists is one where the
cycle just repeats itself over and over

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:51.029
again. the alternate ending that a lot of
people thought they saw coming whenever

00:09:51.029 --> 00:09:55.620
Jonas and Martha entered the origin
reality was that they are the ones who

00:09:55.620 --> 00:10:00.180
caused the crash and thus the cycle was
just bigger than what we could see or

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:05.339
the loop I guess. but I think in the end
this is more satisfying. it uses the

00:10:05.339 --> 00:10:09.990
concepts they introduced in season 3 to
get around the grandfather paradox and

00:10:09.990 --> 00:10:14.339
even though the characters who were born
of the knot no longer exist all of what

00:10:14.339 --> 00:10:17.699
they went through wasn't for nothing. the
group of characters we have at that

00:10:17.699 --> 00:10:23.069
dinner table continued to exist and Tannhaus actually saves his family by

00:10:23.069 --> 00:10:27.750
creating time travel even though he has
no memory of any of that happening. so

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:32.040
with that I'll leave it there there are
a lot of other questions so I'll

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:36.120
probably have some more videos in the
